 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n### InferenceError Raised During Recursion in Inference\n\n#### Description\nIt seems there's an issue with the `raise_if_nothing_inferred` decorator when handling recursion during inference. The problem arises when the recursion limit is hit, leading to an `InferenceError` being raised unexpectedly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\nHere's a snippet to reproduce the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom astroid import nodes\nfrom astroid.exceptions import InferenceError\nfrom astroid.builder import parse\n\n# Simulate a recursion error during inference\n@mock.patch('astroid.nodes.ImportFrom._infer', side_effect=RecursionError)\ndef test_recursion_during_inference(mocked):\n    node = nodes.Call(_extract_single_node('from module import something\\nsomething()'))\n    try:\n        next(node.infer())\n    except InferenceError as error:\n        print(\"Caught InferenceError:\", error)\n\n# Another scenario\ndef test_no_infinite_ancestor_loop():\n    klass = extract_node('import datetime\\ndef method(self):\\n    datetime.datetime = something()\\n\\nclass something(datetime.datetime):\\n    pass')\n    ancestors = [base.name for base in klass.ancestors()]\n    print(\"Ancestors:\", ancestors)\n\n# Regression test for recursion in inference tip\ndef test_recursion_on_inference_tip():\n    code = '''\n    class MyInnerClass: ...\n    class MySubClass: inner_class = MyInnerClass\n    class MyClass: sub_class = MySubClass()\n    def get_unpatched_class(cls): return cls\n    def get_unpatched(item): return get_unpatched_class(item) if isinstance(item, type) else None\n    _Child = get_unpatched(MyClass.sub_class.inner_class)\n    class Child(_Child): def patch(cls): MyClass.sub_class.inner_class = cls\n    '''\n    module = parse(code)\n    print(\"Module parsed:\", module)\n```\n\n#### Expected Results\nThe code should handle recursion gracefully without raising an `InferenceError`.\n\n#### Actual Results\n```python\nInferenceError: Inference failed to find values for the node\n```\n\n#### Additional Information\n- Python version: 3.10.16\n- Platform: Linux\n- Astroid version: [version number]\n- Any other relevant details\n\nIf anyone has insights or suggestions on how to address this, it would be greatly appreciated!\n</issue>\n",
